{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Concerning</b> — Rabbi Marinus said: 'and the white stone became for them a stone instead of a stone,' and likewise concerning evil: entreaties instead of doing good." "<b>The word ויעבתוה</b> — from the root of עבותים. The meaning: if the great one begins to speak, it is from his heart, as it were, [and] those who hear יעבתוה — they make it crooked. The meaning: they add upon them."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "Rabbi Marinus's statement is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. The Hebrew מרינוס may stand for a proper name; no identification attempted.", 1 "The syntax of the second sentence is compressed and the parsing of יעבתוה as a binyan form is uncertain; translated hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:13.827334017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}